## Errors & Mistakes
The first parallel BuildKit check returned before its detached client output was collected, so its result was not usable. Waited for that client to exit and reran the check directly. The first commit also included pre-existing RunAI and ModelScope drift and copied the full NVSHMEM tree. Independent review showed those changes were not part of the v0.27 delta. The commit was amended to remove them. The first NCCL root exposed only nccl.h; source review showed DeepEP runtime JIT also needs nccl_device.h and nccl_device/**, so the amended root exposes the full system include directory. Git automatically copied the old note during amend, so the first reattachment command failed with an existing-note error; this note replaces it. The first serving harness run imported legacy vllm._C, which rc1 no longer ships. The corrected probe imports the stable libtorch extension. The first stable serving run also exposed two harness bugs: it assumed one StatefulSet under the LeaderWorkerSet, and it limited the semantic response to 256 tokens. The corrected harness follows the actual two-StatefulSet ownership chain and allows 512 tokens.

